            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0611" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26496: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Aden
                        (Timberlake)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-15T21:00:00-04:00">December 15,
                            1942—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Your 50, December 15, 11 a.m. The matter is being taken up urgently with the
                    British Government and is being taken up with the <pb facs="0612" n="606"
                        xml:id="pg606"/> British Ambassador here. Therefore please request General
                    Platt to withhold action until such time as a decision is reached and
                    instructions issued to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
